# Enigoma Project

A Go library and CLI implementing a configurable, Unicode-capable Enigma machine.

## Architecture

- `pkg/enigma/` — Public API: `Enigma` struct, functional options, settings serialization, convenience functions, historical variants
- `internal/alphabet/` — Character set management with Unicode support
- `internal/rotor/` — Rotor interface and `BasicRotor` implementation
- `internal/reflector/` — Reflector with reciprocal mapping validation
- `internal/plugboard/` — Plugboard (Steckerbrett) with pair management
- `internal/cli/` — Cobra-based CLI commands (encrypt, decrypt, keygen, wizard, etc.)
- `cmd/enigoma/` — CLI entry point; `cmd/example/` — library usage demo
- `alphabets.go` — Predefined alphabets (Latin, Greek, Cyrillic, Portuguese, ASCII)
- `version.go` — Library version constant

## Key Patterns

- **Functional options**: `enigma.New(WithAlphabet(...), WithRandomSettings(Medium))`
- **Interfaces**: `rotor.Rotor`, `reflector.Reflector` — components are cloneable and serializable
- **Cryptographic randomness**: Always use `crypto/rand` for security-sensitive randomness; `math/rand` only for deterministic seeded modes (mark with `#nosec G404`)
- **Error wrapping**: Use `%w` (not `%v`) in `fmt.Errorf` to preserve error chains
- **Error strings**: Lowercase, no capitalization (Go convention enforced by staticcheck ST1005)

## Commit Messages

- **Short**: one line, max ~50 characters, no body unless strictly necessary
- **No emojis**: never use emojis in commit messages
- **Lowercase start**: begin with a lowercase verb (`fix`, `add`, `update`, `remove`, `refactor`)
- **No trailing period**
- Examples: `fix unicode plugboard deserialization`, `add convenience function tests`

## Development Commands

```
go test ./...                  # Run all tests
go test -race ./...            # Tests with race detector
go vet ./...                   # Static analysis
golangci-lint run              # Lint (v2 config in .golangci.yml)
go build -o bin/enigoma ./cmd/enigoma  # Build CLI
```

